WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.110 --> 00:00:04.840
A message of mRNA is read
three bases at a time.

2
00:00:04.890 --> 00:00:07.850
Group the same bases
starting one letter later,

3
00:00:07.900 --> 00:00:10.370
and every group of three changes.

4
00:00:10.420 --> 00:00:15.100
So where the reading begins decides
every amino acid that follows.

5
00:00:15.150 --> 00:00:20.030
So how does a ribosome find the right
place to start reading a message?

6
00:00:20.080 --> 00:00:24.620
In this mission, you'll see that every
RNA strand has two different ends,

7
00:00:24.670 --> 00:00:26.310
and why that matters.

8
00:00:26.360 --> 00:00:30.770
Then you'll follow the growing
chain as tRNAs bring amino acids,

9
00:00:30.820 --> 00:00:32.740
codon by codon.

10
00:00:32.790 --> 00:00:37.510
Your mission: find out how a ribosome
finds the right place to start reading a

11
00:00:37.560 --> 00:00:38.350
message.
